---
import '../styles/page.css';
import '../styles/inner.css';
import '../styles/platform.css';
import CanvasHero from '../components/CanvasHero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="AI governance built in: how Sparkwing keeps AI trustworthy"
  description="Hive, AI Crew and Control Tower sit under every Sparkwing app, with rules, records and privacy designed in."
>
  <CanvasHero
    scene="trust"
    ground="navy"
    titleId="pf-title"
    label="Animation: sample personal details pass through Control Tower and come out as placeholders before reaching the AI."
  >
    <div class="mx-text" slot="copy">
      <h1 class="mx-h1" id="pf-title">The part you don't see is why you can trust it.</h1>
      <p class="mx-p">
        Every Sparkwing app runs on the same base platform. It comes with every plan, so there is nothing extra to buy.
      </p>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="stage">
      <span class="mx-tile mx-tile--mid" data-tile><img src="/assets/logos/control-tower.svg" alt="" width="60" height="60" /></span>
      <span class="mx-chip mx-at-l0-t18" data-from>Maria Reyes</span>
      <span class="mx-chip mx-at-l0-t48" data-from>maria@email.test</span>
      <span class="mx-chip mx-at-l0-t78" data-from>+63 900 000 0000</span>
      <span class="mx-chip mx-at-r0-t18" data-to>[CUSTOMER 1]</span>
      <span class="mx-chip mx-at-r0-t48" data-to>[EMAIL 1]</span>
      <span class="mx-chip mx-at-r0-t78" data-to>[PHONE 1]</span>
    </Fragment>
  </CanvasHero>

  <section class="sw-band sw-band--surface" aria-label="Base platform">
    <div class="pf-panels">
      <div class="pf-panel pf-panel--hive" id="hive">
        <span class="pf-tag">Knows the business</span>
        <h2>
          <img src="/assets/logos/hive.svg" alt="" width="52" height="52" />Hive
        </h2>
        <p>
          The business context layer under every app: your clients, documents, rules and records, kept in one knowledge library. The AI searches it, so answers come from your own information. It is kept separate from every other client.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="pf-panel pf-panel--crew" id="ai-crew">
        <span class="pf-tag"><span>Does the work</span><span>Coming soon</span></span>
        <h2>
          <img src="/assets/logos/ai-crew.svg" alt="" width="52" height="52" />AI Crew
        </h2>
        <p>The AI tooling that does the work: specialists and bots, like an inbox sorter or a report writer. You choose which helpers your team gets.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pf-panel pf-panel--tower" id="control-tower">
        <span class="pf-tag">Decides what's allowed</span>
        <h2>
          <img src="/assets/logos/control-tower.svg" alt="" width="52" height="52" />Control Tower
        </h2>
        <p>Governance and guardrails. It decides what's allowed and keeps a record of what the AI did.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sw-band" aria-labelledby="pii-title">
    <div class="sw-band-inner sw-stack">
      <div class="pf-pii-head">
        <h2 class="sw-h2" id="pii-title">Names, contact details, and ID, tax and account numbers stay out of the AI.</h2>
        <p>
          They stay inside your own space, kept separate from every other client.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sw-band sw-band--surface" aria-labelledby="who-title">
    <div class="sw-band-inner sw-stack">
      <h2 class="sw-h2" id="who-title">Who will be managing the apps?</h2>
      <div class="pf-who">
        <div class="pf-who-card pf-who-card--rec">
          <span class="pf-who-tag">Recommended</span>
          <h3>Managed by Sparkwing</h3>
          <p>
            We set up users, licences and settings. Your team logs in and works. You get a monthly usage report and regular check-ins.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-who-card">
          <span class="pf-who-tag">For teams with in-house IT</span>
          <h3>Self-managed</h3>
          <p>
            Your IT adds and removes staff and watches usage and cost. We are there when you need support. Either way, the safety rules always stay on.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
